@dataclass(slots=True, kw_only=True)
class AffinePlacementType:
    """
    A placement takes a standard geometric construction and places it in geographic space.

    It defines a transformation from a constructive parameter space to the co-ordinate space of
    the co-ordinate reference system being used. Parameter spaces in formulae in this
    International Standard are given as (u, v) in 2D and(u, v, w) in 3D. Co-ordinate reference
    systems positions are given in formulae, in this International Standard, by either (x, y) in
    2D, or (x, y, z) in 3D. Affine placements are defined by linear transformations from
    parameter space to the target co-ordiante space. 2-dimensional Cartesian parameter
    space,(u,v) transforms into 3-dimensional co- ordinate reference systems,(x,y,z) by using an
    affine transformation,(u,v)-&gt;(x,y,z) which is defined : x ux vx x0 u y = uy vy + y0 v x
    uz vz z0 Then, given this equation, the location element of the AffinePlacement is the
    direct position (x0, y0, z0), which is the target position of the origin in (u, v). The two
    reference directions (ux, uy, uz) and (vx, vy, vz) are the target directions of the unit
    vectors at the origin in (u, v).

    Attributes:
        location: The location property gives the target of the parameter space origin. This
            is the vector (x0, y0, z0) in the formulae above.
        ref_direction: The attribute refDirection gives the target directions for the co-
            ordinate basis vectors of the parameter space. These are the columns of the
            matrix in the formulae given above. The number of directions given shall be
            inDimension. The dimension of the directions shall be outDimension.
        in_dimension: Dimension of the constructive parameter space.
        out_dimension: Dimension of the co-ordinate space.
    """

    class Meta:
        target_namespace = "http://www.opengis.net/gml"

    location: DirectPositionType = field(
        metadata={
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "http://www.opengis.net/gml",
        }
    )
    ref_direction: list[VectorType] = field(
        default_factory=list,
        metadata={
            "name": "refDirection",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "http://www.opengis.net/gml",
            "min_occurs": 1,
        },
    )
    in_dimension: int = field(
        metadata={
            "name": "inDimension",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "http://www.opengis.net/gml",
        }
    )
    out_dimension: int = field(
        metadata={
            "name": "outDimension",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "http://www.opengis.net/gml",
        }
    )


